# (build 133) A pressed mid-step. The level loop calls ProcessAButtonPress
# (ps2.asm:19781) every frame and it never looks at the party's step; the
# target test, Level_ChkTargetInteract (10503), puts loc_7278's box for the
# leader's facing about his pixel position and overlaps it with each
# person's own box. From Aukba 11,9 a step up toward the Dezolian at 11,7
# (dezolis_talk's), A five pixels into it: the box ahead (y 123..138)
# already reaches his (112..127), and he answers -- $1651, Rolf with no
# cap. The step runs on to 11,8 under the window. Until build 133 the port
# held an A on foot back to the end of the step ("ignored: mid-step" under
# PS2_ATRACE) and nothing came up.

start level 10 11 9          # Aukba, two cells below $67 at 11,7
wait screen level
wait idle
walk up 1                    # the step to 11,8 begins
wait ticks 3
press a                      # five pixels into it
wait idle
expect script $1651
expect level 10 11 8
shot 01_answered
press c
wait idle
expect level 10 11 8
